WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.674
A trust lets you decide who gets what, and when.

00:00:04.724 --> 00:00:07.089
You put money or property into the trust.

00:00:07.289 --> 00:00:11.170
A trustee you choose manages it, for the people you want to benefit.

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:19.707
Families use trusts for children, for someone on disability support, for a home or a cottage, or to plan their estate.

00:00:20.757 --> 00:00:28.853
Setting up a trust with Titled costs $2,999, done by a lawyer licensed in Ontario.

00:00:29.052 --> 00:00:34.945
Costs like land transfer tax, if a property moves in, are separate. The lawyer tells you first.

00:00:35.995 --> 00:00:37.639
Tell us what the trust is for.

00:00:37.839 --> 00:00:43.619
A partner lawyer calls within two business days, explains your options, and sets it up with you.
